# Who gets asked to review what.
#
# GitHub requires review from a code owner before a PR can merge (branch
# protection enforces it). The point is not ceremony: it is that the person
# who knows a file is the person who sees the change to it.
#
# Handles are GitHub *teams* in the two-gaming org, not individuals, so a
# review request never dies because one account is asleep. Teams are created
# once by the org owner; see docs/GITHUB.md for the list and who is in each.

# Default: everything in this repo belongs to the bot owner.
*                           @two-gaming/founding-engineer

# Tests and CI are QA's call as well as the bot owner's. Both must approve,
# because "make CI green" is the single easiest thing to get wrong on purpose.
/test/                      @two-gaming/founding-engineer @two-gaming/qa
/.github/workflows/         @two-gaming/founding-engineer @two-gaming/qa

# The contract the website reads. A change here can break two-web silently,
# so the Web Lead sees it before it lands.
/docs/EVENTS.md             @two-gaming/founding-engineer @two-gaming/web-lead

# Secrets, privacy and deploy posture. Changes here are reviewed, always.
/docs/SECRETS.md            @two-gaming/founding-engineer
/docs/PRIVACY.md            @two-gaming/founding-engineer
/deploy/                    @two-gaming/founding-engineer
/.gitignore                 @two-gaming/founding-engineer
/.env.example               @two-gaming/founding-engineer
